WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.038 --> 00:00:07.679
Aunt Polly sent Nancy to deliver the bad news to Mr. Pendleton.

2
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.963
Normally Nancy would have been excited to see inside his mysterious mansion.

3
00:00:12.964 --> 00:00:19.825
But now she was too upset to even glance around the library, where she waited for Mr. Pendleton.

4
00:00:19.826 --> 00:00:23.232
"Well?" he said upon entering the room.

5
00:00:23.233 --> 00:00:29.804
"Sir, the New York doctor says Pollyanna will never walk again!"

6
00:00:29.805 --> 00:00:33.244
Mr. Pendleton sank into the nearest chair.

7
00:00:33.245 --> 00:00:40.412
"Poor little girl." He covered his eyes with his hand and moaned.

8
00:00:40.413 --> 00:00:46.931
"My little prism girl! She'll never dance in the sunshine again."

9
00:00:46.932 --> 00:00:53.918
Nancy could not believe that John Pendleton—a grumpy miser—was showing such emotion. He

10
00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:59.359
looked up. "I hope Pollyanna doesn't know this horrible news." "That's

11
00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:09.534
the worst part, sir. She does." Nancy sobbed. "And

12
00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:14.135
she can't think of anything to be glad about." "I

13
00:01:14.136 --> 00:01:18.181
know how much she loves to play her Glad Game." "I

14
00:01:18.182 --> 00:01:24.271
tried to cheer her up by reminding her what she told Mrs. Snow. But

15
00:01:24.272 --> 00:01:29.337
she said it's one thing to tell a lifelong invalid how to play the game. And

16
00:01:29.338 --> 00:01:34.597
quite another when you're the lifelong invalid." Mr. Pendleton

17
00:01:34.598 --> 00:01:40.336
offered Nancy his handkerchief, and she wiped her eyes before continuing. "Thank you,

18
00:01:40.337 --> 00:01:46.217
sir. Pollyanna used to say the game was more interesting when it was hard. But now

19
00:01:46.218 --> 00:01:52.190
she keeps dwelling on the fact that she'll never walk again. I must

20
00:01:52.191 --> 00:01:57.043
leave, sir, because Miss Polly needs me at home." Nancy hopped

21
00:01:57.044 --> 00:02:00.558
up but turned at the door. "Pollyanna feels

22
00:02:00.559 --> 00:02:04.975
bad that she can't bring Jimmy Bean to visit you. She fears

23
00:02:04.976 --> 00:02:10.614
he didn't make a good impression the first time." She hesitated. "I'm sure

24
00:02:10.615 --> 00:02:14.806
she'd be glad to hear that you were going to visit him." Mr. Pendleton

25
00:02:14.807 --> 00:02:22.347
shook his head. "I'm sorry, but I have no plans to see him." *** The

26
00:02:22.348 --> 00:02:26.832
entire town soon knew that Pollyanna would never walk again. Many

27
00:02:26.833 --> 00:02:32.144
people recognized Pollyanna as the cheerful girl who always greeted them with a smile. And

28
00:02:32.145 --> 00:02:37.381
almost everyone was familiar with the Glad Game. Aunt

29
00:02:37.382 --> 00:02:44.037
Polly was surprised by the number of visitors—friends and strangers—who arrived at her door. Many

30
00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:52.542
people were in tears as they handed Aunt Polly flowers or other gifts for Pollyanna. When

31
00:02:52.543 --> 00:02:57.945
John Pendleton arrived one day, he had an important message for Pollyanna. "Please

32
00:02:57.946 --> 00:03:00.912
tell her that I've seen Jimmy Bean. She'll

33
00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:04.376
be glad to know that I'm thinking of adopting him." Aunt

34
00:03:04.377 --> 00:03:08.712
Polly was so shocked that she couldn't control her reaction. "Jimmy

35
00:03:08.713 --> 00:03:17.421
Bean?" she gasped. "You're going to adopt that . . . that boy?" "Yes,

36
00:03:17.422 --> 00:03:22.570
and I think Pollyanna will understand why." After

37
00:03:22.571 --> 00:03:27.766
Mr. Pendleton left, Aunt Polly went upstairs and delivered his message. "Mr.

38
00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:32.418
Pendleton said you'd be glad about this news." Pollyanna

39
00:03:32.419 --> 00:03:35.627
broke into a wide grin. "Glad?

40
00:03:35.628 --> 00:03:44.088
Of course I'm glad! Oh, Aunt Polly, I've wanted to find a place for Jimmy to live. And

41
00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:48.848
Mr. Pendleton's house is such a lovely place. Besides,

42
00:03:48.849 --> 00:03:55.322
I'm glad for Mr. Pendleton because he'll have a child's presence." "A

43
00:03:55.323 --> 00:03:57.103
what?" "Mr.

44
00:03:57.104 --> 00:04:04.197
Pendleton thinks it takes a spouse's hand and heart or a child's presence to make a house a home. Dr.

45
00:04:04.198 --> 00:04:07.182
Chilton thinks that too." Aunt

46
00:04:07.183 --> 00:04:14.891
Polly looked startled. " Dr. Chilton ! How do you know what he

47
00:04:14.892 --> 00:04:23.034
thinks?" "He told me himself. He says the rooms where he lives aren't really a home."

48
00:04:23.035 --> 00:04:28.015
While Aunt Polly stared silently out the window, Pollyanna went on.

49
00:04:28.016 --> 00:04:32.471
"So I asked him why he didn't get a spouse's hand and heart."

50
00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:40.892
"Pollyanna!" Aunt Polly turned abruptly and shook her finger at Pollyanna. "Why did you do that?"

51
00:04:40.893 --> 00:04:44.686
"Because he seemed so sad."

52
00:04:44.687 --> 00:04:48.248
There was another question that Aunt Polly wanted to ask.

53
00:04:48.249 --> 00:04:54.185
She hesitated, almost afraid to hear the answer.

54
00:04:54.186 --> 00:05:00.071
She sat down and gathered her courage before asking, "What did he say?"

55
00:05:00.072 --> 00:05:04.709
"He said you can't always get a spouse just by asking.

56
00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:11.103
I know he wants a wife because I heard him say so, even though he spoke very quietly."

57
00:05:11.104 --> 00:05:16.688
"What did he say?" Aunt Polly asked again in her own soft voice.

58
00:05:16.689 --> 00:05:23.457
"He said he'd do almost anything to have one particular woman's hand and heart."

59
00:05:23.458 --> 00:05:27.618
Aunt Polly stood up hurriedly and went back to the window.

60
00:05:27.619 --> 00:05:30.554
"What's the matter, Aunt Polly?"

61
00:05:30.555 --> 00:05:40.955
"Er . . . nothing, dear. It's time to move this pendant so it catches more light."

